  {"i":755,"t":["qualities"],"s":{"2":["actions"]},"n":"Being lucky (ついてる) is a state of fortune, not an emotion; the 'attached' sense goes to actions."},
  {"i":761,"t":["work","school"],"n":"ミス(をする) is taught with workplace errors and test mistakes; it is a noun, not a describing word."},
  {"i":794,"t":["food","shopping"],"s":{"2":["actions"],"4":["sports"]},"n":"First met as a set meal or combo (ランチセット) and as a set of goods; numbers does not fit."},
  {"i":804,"t":["qualities","function"],"n":"Learners meet もの first as 'thing' (N5), but the ～もの/ものだ formal-noun patterns are core N3 grammar."},
  {"i":814,"t":["relationships"],"n":"Meeting people is social contact; actions adds nothing a teacher would use."},
  {"i":839,"t":["drink","health"],"n":"薬を飲む is a standard phrase in the health unit, alongside the drinking sense."},
  {"i":848,"t":["health","greetings","feelings"],"n":"Healthy and lively, and お元気ですか is a core beginner greeting."},
  {"i":850,"t":["time","numbers"],"n":"Once or one time is a frequency word, so time comes first."},
