 "d": [
  {"i":755,"keep":[],"n":"'Attached / comes with' is common, but it is just the te-iru form of 付く and would be taught with that verb, not in an actions unit."},
  {"i":778,"keep":[],"n":"At this level ファン means enthusiast. An electric fan is 扇風機, and the device sense of ファン is rare for learners."},
  {"i":794,"keep":[2,4],"n":"セットする (set an alarm, set up) is common for general actions, and a set in volleyball or tennis is commonly taught with sports."},
  {"i":819,"keep":[2],"n":"料理を作る and ご飯を作る are core food-unit vocabulary."},
  {"i":822,"keep":[2],"n":"いえ as family or household (家の人, 家族) is common and fits the family unit."},
  {"i":833,"keep":[4],"n":"体にいい and 体に気をつけて are standard health phrases."},
  {"i":843,"keep":[3],"n":"'To occur' (事故が起きる) is a very common N4-N3 sense and lies outside routine. It is a general verb, so it goes under actions."},
  {"i":844,"keep":[3],"n":"The 〜方 suffix for 'way of doing' (読み方, 使い方) is a core grammar pattern."},
  {"i":846,"keep":[2],"n":"Social issues such as 環境問題 and 社会問題 are common N3 vocabulary for the society unit."},
  {"i":853,"keep":[2],"n":"Seeing someone off or taking them somewhere (駅まで送る) is common and is a movement sense."},
  {"i":856,"keep":[2],"n":"Parking (車を止める) is common and taught in the transport unit."},
  {"i":869,"keep":[],"n":"'Breakfast' for 朝 alone is colloquial. Learners use 朝ご飯 or 朝食 instead."},
  {"i":885,"keep":[2],"n":"'How many degrees' (今日は何度?) is common in weather talk and with temperature units."},
  {"i":886,"keep":[3,4],"n":"Switching off devices (電気/スイッチを切る) and hanging up (電話を切る) are both common senses, each taught in its own unit."}
 ]
